WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
A dark forest.

2
00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:04.630
Two eyes, burning bright.

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.390
"In the forests of the
night," Then a workshop:

4
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.220
a hammer, a chain, a furnace, an anvil.

5
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.330
Each with a question mark.

6
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.330
At the edge of the frame, a small lamb.

7
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.540
Did the same hand make both?

8
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.240
Almost the whole poem is questions.

9
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.290
Does Blake ever answer them?

10
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.590
In this mission, you'll face the Tyger,
which William Blake published in Songs

11
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.610
of Experience, in 1794.

12
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.240
You'll step into the
maker's forge, tool by tool.

13
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.650
And you'll set it beside its partner poem,

14
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.210
The Lamb, from Songs of Innocence.

15
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.120
Your mission: decide whether
Blake answers his questions.
